From b5296eeb81ed17904711672b0b99977e0d6e0704 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Florian Stosse <1315-Harvester57@users.noreply.git.frama-c.com>
Date: Tue, 17 Nov 2026 18:30:13 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] [e-acsl] compute the zone sizes of --zone-sizes in size_t

e-acsl-gcc --zone-sizes passes each size, in MB, to the runtime as a macro
(E_ACSL_HEAP_SIZE, E_ACSL_STACK_SIZE, E_ACSL_TLS_SIZE,
E_ACSL_THREAD_STACK_SIZE). The segment model converted it to bytes with
`size * MB`, where MB is the int constant 1024 * 1024, so from 2048 MB on
the product overflowed int (gcc: "integer overflow in expression of type
'int' results in '-2147483648'"). Converted to size_t, the result was
either huge or wrapped modulo 4 GB: heap:2048 to heap:4095 and stack:2048
crashed every run at start-up, heap:4096 aborted at the first malloc,
heap:4097 gave a 1 MB heap, and thread-stack:2048 made pthread_create fail.

Convert the size to size_t before the multiplication, at the places where
it is turned into bytes.

New test special/e-acsl-zone-sizes.c: a program run with
--zone-sizes heap:2048,stack:2048 (dev configuration).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
